Apple today released <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-26/">macOS Tahoe</a> 26.4, the fourth major update to the &zwnj;macOS Tahoe&zwnj; operating system. &zwnj;macOS Tahoe&zwnj; comes six weeks after Apple released &zwnj;macOS Tahoe&zwnj; 26.3.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1006759" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/06/macOS-Tahoe-26-Thumb-2.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" /><br/>
Mac users can download the new software by opening up the System Settings app and navigating to the Software Update section.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;macOS Tahoe&zwnj; 26.4 returns the compact tab bar option to Safari for those who prefer the slimmed down look, along with a new Charge Limit feature for the Mac so you can set a maximum charge level from 80 to 100 percent. It also adds new eight emoji characters, and it displays warnings for apps that will stop working in the future. Apple is ending support for Rosetta 2 after <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS 27</a>, so app that are still using Rosetta will display a popup letting users know that the app won't work starting with macOS 28.<br/>
<br/>
